worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_statistics.js"
  ceiling 1070
  rationale "Statistics over stated number lists, and the price-times-count word problems that share their vocabulary (issue #1176). JavaScript-first twin of native handler keys (statistics, word_problem), added under R997-R999 (2026-10-06); growth is the ported handler, not silent regrowth. Ceiling moved 832 to 956 for the percentile twin (R1176-3, 2026-10-07): exact linear interpolation between closest ranks and the rank-parameter reader. Ceiling moved 956 to 1041 for the primality twin (R1017, 2026-10-07): one stated whole number tested by trial division up to its integer square root, twin of rust/src/solver_handlers/statistics/primality.rs. Ceiling moved 1041 to 1043 for the relation fallback (R1176-2, 2026-10-07): an unmatched unit-price pattern hands the prompt to tryRelationWordProblem in formal_ai_worker_word_relations.js. Ceiling moved 1043 to 1070: tryOneItemChange answers the one-item change word problem (a payment and a price, no unit price; issue #1175 p350, 2026-10-08), the twin of one_item_change in rust/src/solver_handlers/statistics.rs."
